## The Headless CMS Dilemma

Most modern headless CMS setups come with overhead: database hosting, API limits, monthly subscription fees, and complex auth flows just to edit a personal blog.

By switching to **Astro Content Collections** paired with **Keystatic**:

- **No Remote Database**: Every blog post, case study, and project is a Markdown/Markdoc file directly version-controlled in your Git repository.
- **Local Visual Editing**: Running `astro dev` boots up Keystatic's rich visual text editor on `localhost:4321/keystatic`.
- **Zero Cost & Sub-Millisecond Speed**: When you push your code, static compilation pre-renders every page into plain HTML/CSS/JS, deployed globally on Cloudflare Pages or GitHub Pages for free.

It's the ultimate setup for builders who want to write without managing server infrastructure.
